{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Excellence of exaltation and excellence of might — impetuous as water, do not excel.</b> You are impetuous as water; do not excel over your brothers in the matter of 'excellence of exaltation,' which is the prerogative of exaltation and receiving an extra portion in the priesthood and the birthright — even though you are <b>the first of my strength</b> and were worthy of the right of the firstborn, as it says: כִּי הוּא רֵאשִׁית אוֹנוֹ (Deuteronomy 21:17)." "<b>And excellence of might.</b> Nor shall you <b>excel</b> in the prerogative of might, which is kingship — being mightier and more powerful than any other in his kingdom, as our Sages of blessed memory said: אֵין עֹז אֶלָּא מַלְכוּת. This too is fitting for the firstborn, as it says: וְאֶת הַמַּמְלָכָה נָתַן לִיהוֹרָם כִּי הוּא הַבְּכוֹר (II Chronicles 21:3)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:14.598099246Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}